  "_doc_drift": "Drift is against the fixed round-0 records iter_00/bench.json + iter_00/suite.json, same case and precision (v1.14, v1.17). abs_err_max rel 0.5 = at most 1.5x the round-0 record: a gross single-element check, not a band check (v1.16). spread_ratio_p50 two-sided: +-0.005 accuracy, +-0.01 performance (v1.11). Floors set by D2 item 6.",
  "_doc_f2": "D3 item 1: f2_* is forward 2, teacher-forced on the reference's forward-1 median (long_horizon in the bench, horizon4 in the suite); every forward-1 floor and drift applies with the f2_ prefix, except pcc_final/pcc_final_spread (the bench gates the end-to-end forecast once, as forward 1's). long_horizon gets case floors for its narrower forward-2 bands: iter_00/floors_g1.md 'Forward 2'.",
  "_doc_bias": "D3 item 3: bias_row_max (any row) and bias_row_p95 (>= 100 rows) catch a shift on a minority of rows; floors at about 1.3-1.5x the round-0 maximum per case, drift x1.5 (max) and +0.005 (p95)."
